=== SURVEY ===
Web source CopyLinkButton.tsx = a single ghost/sm Button that copies the current URL
(window.location.href, path + query) to the clipboard so a filtered / deep-linked view can be
shared, then shows a transient confirmation + a toast:
  • icon swaps Link2 → Check while `copied`; label swaps "Copy link" → "Copied".
  • on success: navigator.clipboard.writeText (with a textarea/execCommand fallback for non-secure
    contexts), setCopied(true), toast.success("Link copied to clipboard"),
    setTimeout(setCopied(false), 2000).
  • on failure (catch): toast.error("Could not copy link").
  • aria-label = "Copy link to this view".
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation (P1/S10 facade), useToast (toast seam). Ambient:
window.location.href. NO network and NO data-fetch state holder. Shared components: ui/Button.
Charts/maps: none.
Closest committed precedent studied: shared-surfaces/ChartExportMenu (0066) — the sibling
props-driven action surface that also binds only useTranslation + a toast seam and copies to the
clipboard; same architecture + same "reproduce the web's real branches (no fabricated data-feed
states)" disposition, and the same P4-apple DEFERRED-xcodebuild gate disposition.

=== REASONING ===
- Architecture mirrors the props-driven leaf precedent (no Adapter/Projection because there is no
  data feed — only the localisation facade, a toast seam, the ambient URL, and the clipboard):
  • Model (Foundation/Observation/OSLog): CopyLinkButtonCopyOutcome (web try/catch);
    CopyLinkButtonToastSeverity/Intent; CopyLinkButtonLogic (pure — toastIntent mapping, the
    icon switch link/checkmark, the label switch, canCopy guard, url+clipboard→outcome);
    CopyLinkButtonMeta (slug "CopyLinkButton"); CopyLinkButtonTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) +
    OSLog default + Diagnostics seam; CopyLinkButtonToastPresenter (native useToast — @MainActor
    AnyObject, optional for graceful degrade); CopyLinkButtonStrings (P1/S10 facade); @MainActor
    @Observable CopyLinkButtonModel (owns the URL provider + clipboard + optional toast + the
    transient `copied`; copyLink() = the verbatim web handleClick; markAppeared() emits view.opened
    once; 2s auto-revert via an injectable autoResetDelay).
  • Seams: CopyLinkURLProviding (native window.location.href — synchronous getter; Static + Resolving
    sources) + CopyLinkClipboard (UIPasteboard/NSPasteboard SystemCopyLinkClipboard + InMemory double
    for previews/tests).
  • swift (the View): TSButton(.ghost,.small) bound through the model; designated + closure-wiring
    inits; disabled when no shareable URL; VoiceOver label + value; view.opened onAppear.
  • Views: the label content (SF Symbol + title) with a reduce-motion-gated symbol-replace transition.
  • Previews: resting / copied / copy-demo(toast wired) / unavailable(no URL).
  • strings: the exact 5 web keys; Tests + ModelTests.
- "Every web branch renders" honoured for the control's REAL branches: this is a stateless,
  networkless action surface, so the generic loading/empty/error/stale/offline template states do
  not exist in the web source — faithful parity = reproducing the branches that DO exist (action /
  copied / success toast / error toast / native-graceful unavailable), the same precedent as the
  committed sibling ChartExportMenu 0066 (documented in the file headers).
- Side effects off the view: the clipboard write + toast announcement + reset timer live on the
  @MainActor model so no Task-sending / Sendable plumbing leaks into the SwiftUI layer (the project
  builds under SWIFT_STRICT_CONCURRENCY=complete / Swift 6 language mode).
- Rejected: porting the web textarea/execCommand fallback (the platform pasteboard is the native
  equivalent); porting Tailwind/raw hex (used P1/S9 tokens); a literal global "window.location"
  (modelled as an injectable provider seam read fresh at copy time); reusing the atomic
  Sources/Components/UI TSCopyButton (that is a generic value-copy atomic, not this layout-chrome
  share surface with its own i18n keys, toast, telemetry, and aria-label).

